  "description": "WAJFEX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C126 H172 O24 P4 Tb4,4.8(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.603-3.994 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.95-114.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C126H172O24P4Tb4·4.8(C2H6O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
